{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Identity.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Identity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ring identity ring identity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Identity.md","fileName":"Ring Identity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Ring Identity","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ring and Ideal Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Commutative Ring","Ring Homomorphism","Ring Unit","Field","Trivial Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Identity.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Identity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ring identity ring identity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Identity.md","fileName":"Ring Identity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Ring Identity","heading":"Ring Identity","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A ring identity is an element 1 such that multiplying any ring element by 1 leaves it unchanged. In the book's convention, every [[Commutative Ring]] has an identity and every [[Ring Homomorphism]] preserves it.\n\nThe identity distinguishes units: a [[Ring Unit]] is an element that can be multiplied by another element to obtain 1. A nonzero [[Field]] requires its identity to be distinct from zero.\n\nThe source writes the ring identity as 1_A to keep track of the ambient ring. It also singles out the [[Trivial Ring]], where 0_A = 1_A, before defining characteristics and nontrivial domains.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Commutative Ring","Ring Homomorphism","Ring Unit","Field","Trivial Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}